# Query functions {#sec-api-query}

Expressions (`Expr`) are the predicates and derived columns you pass to
[`Frame.filter`](api-frame.tmd#fn-filter) and the other query methods. Build them from the
helpers below.

## `col` {#fn-col}

```python
col(name: str) -> Expr
```

Reference a column by name inside a query. Compare or combine the result to form a
predicate: `col("year") >= 2020`, or `col("a") + col("b")` for a derived column.

- **name** — the column to reference.
- **Returns** — an `Expr` you can compare, combine, and pass to a query method.

## `lit` {#fn-lit}

```python
lit(value) -> Expr
```

Wrap a Python scalar as an `Expr`, for the rare case where a bare literal is ambiguous
(for instance the right-hand side of a `.otherwise(lit(0))`).

- **value** — any Python scalar.
- **Returns** — a constant `Expr`.

::: {.callout-warning title="Deprecated since v0.5"}
`Frame.where()` is deprecated and will be removed in v1.0. Use
[`Frame.filter`](api-frame.tmd#fn-filter) instead: it takes the same predicate and reads
the same way.
:::
